            "id": "4946397",
            "title": "Wall Street Breakfast Podcast: Alarm Bells On Wall Street",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\"><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"S and P 500 index symbol. Wooden blocks with an arrow that symbolizes that the S and P 500 index is changing trend, goes up or down. Business concept. Copy space.\" data-id=\"2170830123\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1024\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2170830123/image_2170830123.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">Andrzej Rostek/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>Download this episode on<a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/wall-street-breakfast/id1358381502\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"> Apple Podcasts</a>/<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/05uLjJxkVgQsRk8LWLCLpx?si=r3_yJgxiQiivJwNQG8WNew&amp;nd=1\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Spotify</a> or listen below:</p> <p></p><div class=\"pcast hidden-print\">\n<div class=\"pcast__section-1\">\n<img alt=\"\" class=\"pcast__top-img pcast__marketing\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2018/11/21/podcast_series_header.png?io=w640\"/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pcast__section-2\"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"200px\" sap-id=\"4\" src=\"https://widget.spreaker.com/player?episode_id=75144172&amp;theme=light&amp;playlist=false&amp;playlist-continuous=false&amp;chapters-image=true&amp;episode_image_position=right&amp;hide-logo=true&amp;hide-likes=true&amp;hide-comments=true&amp;hide-sharing=true&amp;hide-download=true&amp;color=ff6900\" title=\"Alarm bells on Wall Street\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></div>\n<div class=\"pcast__section-3\">\n<div class=\"pcast__ad-container\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>One Wall Street firm sees a <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642742-sp-500-faces-8-10-pullback-risk-as-fed-rate-hikes-loom-strategist-says\">painful replay</a> of 2018 for stocks (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500\" title=\"S&amp;P 500 Index\">SP500</a>). (00:15) Verizon (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VZ\" title=\"Verizon Communications Inc.\">VZ</a>) and T-Mobile (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TMUS\" title=\"T-Mobile US, Inc.\">TMUS</a>) are finally <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642631-verizon-t-mobile-end-legal-fight-over-competing-savings-claims\">calling a truce</a> in their ad war. (02:26) One Costco (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COST\" title=\"Costco Wholesale Corporation\">COST</a>) staple just got a lot <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642623-costco-hikes-motor-oil-prices-and-limits-purchases\">more expensive</a>—and harder to buy. (02:59)</p> <p>This is an abridged transcript.</p> <p>Macro Risk Advisors LLC is saying potential Federal Reserve rate hikes starting this week could trigger an 8% to 10% correction in the S&amp;P 500 (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link%7Cfirst_level_url%3Anews\">SP500</a>).</p> <p>Dean Curnutt, chief executive officer and founder of Macro Risk Advisors said, “We expect an 8-10% pullback in S&amp;P with a potential second leg in December,” in a Monday note to clients, according to Bloomberg.</p> <p>Curnutt added, rate hikes will “compress margins in companies that cannot pass costs through” and deliver a volatility shock to a market that is not positioned for it.</p> <p>The S&amp;P 500 has fallen nearly 1% so far in September, historically its weakest month, amid concerns over elevated energy costs and recent inflation data that pushed the 10-year U.S. Treasury yield to its highest level in nearly two decades.</p> <p>Traders are now almost fully pricing in a quarter-point rate hike by Fed Chairman Kevin Warsh on Wednesday, up from about 60% odds a week ago. Curnutt said, a rate hike on Wednesday is likely to lead to more pain.</p> <p>Curnutt said the current setup resembles 2018, when the S&amp;P 500 peaked in September before plunging 10% over October and November. That year, Curnutt warned, “The Santa Claus rally did not come,” and the market took another leg lower in December, eventually falling nearly 20% from its peak.</p> <p>Given that history, “a defensive posture is the correct approach,” he said. Similar to 2018, he expects the market to take another leg lower in December as multiple Fed hikes hit “into a K-shaped, low-churn economy.”</p> <p>The S&amp;P 500 is heavily concentrated in mega-cap technology and AI-related stocks, with Nvidia (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NVDA\" title=\"NVIDIA Corporation\">NVDA</a>), Apple (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AAPL\" title=\"Apple Inc.\">AAPL</a>), Microsoft (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MSFT\" title=\"Microsoft Corporation\">MSFT</a>), Amazon (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMZN\" title=\"Amazon.com, Inc.\">AMZN</a>), Alphabet (GOOGL/GOOG), Broadcom (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AVGO\" title=\"Broadcom Inc.\">AVGO</a>), Meta Platforms (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/META\" title=\"Meta Platforms, Inc.\">META</a>), and Tesla (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TSLA\" title=\"Tesla, Inc.\">TSLA</a>) among its largest constituents.</p> <p>NVDA has fallen over 4% so far in September, AMZN is down 2.4%, AVGO is down 6.9%, and TSLA has dipped 2.4%. AAPL is up 5%, while GOOG has gained 3% in the month so far.</p> <p>Verizon Wireless (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VZ\" title=\"Verizon Communications Inc.\">VZ</a>) and T-Mobile US (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TMUS\" title=\"T-Mobile US, Inc.\">TMUS</a>) have agreed to end their legal battle.</p> <p>The two companies have been in litigation over advertising campaigns that each company said misled consumers about the savings available when switching wireless providers.</p> <p>They filed an agreement Friday in Manhattan federal court seeking dismissal of Verizon’s lawsuit and T-Mobile’s countersuit, bringing the dispute to a close after months of litigation.</p> <p>Discussions between the carriers had also explored ways to handle similar advertising disputes in the future.</p> <p>Costco Wholesale (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COST\" title=\"Costco Wholesale Corporation\">COST</a>) has sharply raised the price of its Kirkland Signature full-synthetic motor oil and introduced purchase limits.</p> <p>The 10-quart package, which contains two 5-quart bottles, now sells for about $57.99, almost double the prior range of $30 to $35.</p> <p>Members are generally limited to two packages per week, with some local listings indicating a limit of one purchase at a time. Costco (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COST\" title=\"Costco Wholesale Corporation\">COST</a>) has also reportedly imposed limits on Mobil 1 full-synthetic six-quart packs, which sell for around $44.</p> <p>The move is unusual for the retailer since bulk availability is in its DNA. Repercussions from rising crude oil prices and broader lubricant shortages associated with disruptions in petroleum markets and shipping are believed to have factored into the price boost.</p> <p>What’s Trending on Seeking Alpha:</p> <p><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642737-us-has-weapons-in-space-air-force-secretary-confirms\">U.S. has weapons in space, Air Force secretary confirms</a></p> <p><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642713-chevron-ceo-wirth-other-us-oil-executives-warn-global-fuel-crisis-has-arrived\">Chevron CEO Wirth, other U.S. oil executives warn global fuel crisis has arrived</a></p> <p><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642740-us-10-year-treasury-yield-climbs-to-highest-level-since-2007-ahead-of-fed-decision\">U.S. 10-year Treasury yield climbs to highest level since 2007 ahead of Fed decision</a></p> <p>Catalyst watch:</p> <ul> <li><p>Marvel's Wolverine videogame will be released. Disney-owned (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/DIS\" title=\"The Walt Disney Company\">DIS</a>) Marvel is releasing the game exclusively on Sony's (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SONY\" title=\"Sony Group Corporation\">SONY</a>) PlayStation 5.</p></li> <li><p>Corteva (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CTVA\" title=\"Corteva, Inc.\">CTVA</a>) will hold an investor day event to discuss the separation of its advanced seed and genetics business into a standalone, publicly traded company called Vylor.</p></li> </ul> <p>Stock index futures are in the red.</p> <p>Crude oil is up 2.6% at $104. Brent crude is up 2.4% at $108.</p> <p>The FTSE 100 is down 0.7% and the DAX is down 0.6%.</p> <p>One stock on the <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642746-biggest-stock-movers-tuesday-play-enva-and-more\">biggest movers</a> list: Dave &amp; Buster's Entertainment (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PLAY\" title=\"Dave &amp; Buster's Entertainment, Inc.\">PLAY</a>) -14% - Shares plunged after higher food and beverage, payroll, and pre-opening costs pushed the entertainment and restaurant operator to an unexpected Q2 loss.</p> <p>Economic calendar:</p> <ul><li><p>FOMC meeting begins</p></li></ul></body></html>",
